<title>USA: US lawmakers propose blocking China MFN extension.</title>
<headline>US lawmakers propose blocking China MFN extension.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Senate Foreign Relations Committee chairman Jesse Helms and three other senators on Tuesday introduced a resolution to block the extension of Most Favored Nation trade status for China.</p>
<p>President Bill Clinton has requested extension of MFN trade status for China and it can only be denied if the disapproval resolution passes both the House and Senate over his veto. MFN trade status confers normal trading rights upon a country.</p>
<p>Helms, a North Carolina Republican, objected to MFN for China because of the country's record on human rights.</p>
</text>
